[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A manager or supervisor agent coordinates specialized subagents, delegates the relevant parts of a task, sequences their work, and synthesizes their outputs. Separate tool lists and nonshared conversation histories indicate isolated context for each subagent, rather than a shared-context manager pattern or a pipeline that passes the full history between stages. Anthropic’s guidance identifies isolated context and independent workstreams as appropriate uses for subagents.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A robust session lifecycle defines per-session expiration rules, explicit triggers that clear session state, and conditions for beginning a new session. Together, these controls prevent stale conversational context from leaking into subsequent conversations.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude requests must be sent through Amazon Bedrock to meet the contractual routing requirement. Anthropic supports invoking Claude on Bedrock through its Bedrock integration and SDKs, allowing the application’s higher-level Claude interaction logic to remain decoupled from the underlying provider while the configured invocation path uses Bedrock.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A production application proceeds into ongoing operations and maintenance, including monitoring, incident response, and planning or delivering future evolution.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }The project-scoped `.claude/settings.json` file is version-controlled with the repository and shared across collaborators. It supports configuration such as permissions, environment variables, and model defaults, providing consistent project-level Claude Code behavior.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }WebSockets are designed for persistent, bidirectional, real-time communication between a client and a streaming service, avoiding the overhead and latency of repeated polling requests.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Prompt engineering should be an iterative process: update the prompt to improve performance for the growing failure category, validate the update with evaluations that also protect common-case performance, and continue refining based on the results.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude streaming sends Messages API responses incrementally through server-sent events, including text deltas as generation proceeds. This lets an application display output progressively instead of waiting for the completed response.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Separate Claude calls let the triage stage use a focused classification prompt and produce an intermediate result that can be inspected, evaluated, routed, or constrained before a response-specific prompt drafts the reply. Explicit prompt chaining is appropriate when an application needs a defined sequential pipeline and observable intermediate outputs.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Business goals must first be interpreted as functional requirements, such as the agent’s required memo-drafting tasks and user interactions, and infrastructure or nonfunctional requirements, such as performance, security, integration, and reliability constraints. Those requirements provide the basis for later workflow discovery, model selection, and technical scoping.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A prompt-version change can change the output contract, behavior, format, or quality consumed by dependent systems. Each downstream dependency therefore requires an impact assessment before deployment, with coordination from its owners where needed. Anthropic’s evaluation guidance recommends rerunning the full evaluation set after a prompt update to determine how the new prompt affects performance across test cases.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }The Claude API enforces organization-level limits for requests per minute, input tokens per minute, and output tokens per minute, including over short intervals through a token-bucket mechanism. Applications should identify their applicable limits, keep peak-hour traffic within them, and handle rate-limit responses by waiting and retrying with exponential backoff. A 429 rate-limit response supplies a `retry-after` header indicating when retrying may succeed.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Prompt engineering shapes the instructions, examples, constraints, and output format of an individual model interaction. Context engineering manages the relevant information and state supplied throughout a multi-step, long-horizon workflow, including continuity across turns or context windows, so the model retains the information needed for subsequent work.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Request traces expose the complete context of each refusal, allowing the specific trigger—such as the input pattern, system-prompt content, or other request context—to be identified before making changes or performing aggregate analysis. Claude identifies safety refusals with a `refusal` stop reason, so request-level inspection is the appropriate starting point for diagnosing them.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A model upgrade should be validated with the application’s actual prompts and workload. When a regression is caused by changed response formatting for multi-section system prompts, adapting the prompt to the new model’s documented formatting and instruction conventions, followed by re-evaluation, directly tests whether compatibility can be restored without losing the measured reasoning benefit. Claude’s prompting guidance recommends clear, explicit output requirements and structured prompts for complex instructions, and its migration guidance calls for updating prompts and configurations when moving between model generations.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Project-level `CLAUDE.md` instructions are team-shared through source control, and shared project settings belong with the repository they configure. Keeping both alongside the application source provides one reviewable history and lets standard pull-request controls govern changes to code and its Claude Code configuration.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Multi-shot prompting includes labeled examples in the prompt, allowing Claude to recognize and reproduce the intended output format for each request. Anthropic identifies well-crafted few-shot or multi-shot examples as a reliable way to steer output format and improve consistency.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Format drift in a multi-turn application is addressed by examining how accumulated conversation context affects instruction adherence, managing that context, and validating outputs against the required JSON structure. Explicit output-format constraints and structured prompting help maintain consistent formatting, while validation detects outputs that fail the required schema.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.md` files hierarchically, allowing broadly scoped instructions to provide shared standards and repository-local files to add project-specific rules. This centralizes common guidance without losing repository-specific context.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A primary orchestration layer should govern specialized agents through enforceable per-agent resource limits, structured output validation, and explicit contracts for information passed between stages. These controls prevent unnecessary tool use and token overruns, reject malformed or incompatible outputs before propagation, and make responsibilities and expected data formats clear enough to reduce contradictions.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Full request-and-response traces make runs reproducible and comparable. Recording the input, system prompt, user messages, model output, and parameters exposes hidden contextual or configuration differences that can account for inconsistent behavior. Anthropic’s documentation supports logging and inspecting intermediate API outputs when diagnosing application behavior.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude model selection should satisfy the task’s quality, latency, and cost requirements jointly, because model capability, response time, and token pricing are interdependent tradeoffs. Selecting by one dimension first and evaluating the others only afterward can produce a model that is unsuitable for the overall workload. Anthropic’s model pricing documentation also shows that Claude models have materially different costs, reinforcing that cost must be considered alongside performance requirements.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Code supports non-interactive/headless execution with print mode (`-p`) for scripts and CI pipelines. Preconfiguring the permitted tools in `settings.json` allows the defined actions to run without manual approval, and JSON or stream-JSON output can be captured for downstream processing.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A planned refactoring pass removes the technical debt that is making further development difficult. Consolidating duplicated logic, separating concerns, and simplifying control flow improves maintainability and establishes a safer foundation for new features.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Prompt caching reuses an identical prefix of an API prompt to reduce input-token processing time and cost. The reusable prefix should contain static content that recurs across requests, including system prompts, instructions, shared context, examples, and tool definitions. It does not cache generated model output; application-level response caching is a separate technique.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Tool output pruning removes results that later workflow steps no longer require, preventing obsolete tool-result content from consuming the context window. Tool-result blocks contribute to the input tokens sent to Claude, so caching retained results does not solve context bloat.

